-- Clears cover art too large to read back.
--
-- Android hands query results over through a two-megabyte CursorWindow, and a
-- row too large does not come back short: the read of the whole table throws, so
-- one oversized cover took the entire library off the screen and left a retry
-- button. Covers were stored exactly as rendered or found until this version - a
-- PDF page at its own size, artwork at 1600x2400 - and one image-heavy book
-- passed the limit on its own.
--
-- The limit is `MaxStoredCoverBytes`, what the import now holds new covers to.
-- `length()` on a BLOB counts bytes, so this decodes no artwork to decide.
--
-- Cleared rather than re-made: the cover would have to be rendered from the file
-- again, and a migration runs at startup, on the main thread, for a library
-- whose files may have moved. Those books show the monogram until they are
-- refreshed or imported again.
UPDATE document SET coverImage = NULL WHERE length(coverImage) > 1000000;
